<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulrich, Duke of Württemberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1487">1487</a>–1550</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulrich, Duke of Württemberg, ruled from 1498 to 1550. His heavy taxes provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poor-conrad">Poor Conrad</a> revolt of 1514, and after he seized the imperial city of Reutlingen in 1519 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-league">Swabian League</a> drove him out, leaving the duchy under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule. Restored in 1534 with the help of Philip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, he introduced the Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulrich-duke-of-wurttemberg.jpg" alt="Ulrich, Duke of Württemberg" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:900-121_Herzog_Ulrich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
